"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup on Destroy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the function cancels any pending batch when the component is destroyed.\nUse the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmount"},{"type":"text","value":" option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const batcher = injectBatcher(fn, {\n  maxSize: 5,\n  onUnmount: (b) => b.flush()\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularBatcherOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularBatcherOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularBatcher.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularBatcher"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst batcher = injectBatcher(\n  (items) => console.log('Processing batch:', items),\n  { maxSize: 5, wait: 2000 }\n);\n\n// Add items\nbatcher.addItem('task1');\n\n// Access the selected state\nconst { items, isPending } = batcher.state();","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","text":"Cleanup on Destroy","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction injectBatcher<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): AngularBatcher<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [batcher/injectBatcher.ts:91](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/batcher/injectBatcher.ts#L91)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages a Batcher instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the Batcher's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThe Batcher collects items and processes them in batches based on configurable conditions:\n- Maximum batch size\n- Time-based batching (process after X milliseconds)\n- Custom batch processing logic via getShouldExecute\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function cancels any pending batch when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```ts\nconst batcher = injectBatcher(fn, {\n  maxSize: 5,\n  onUnmount: (b) => b.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `void`\n\n### options?\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularBatcherOptions`](../interfaces/AngularBatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\\> = `{}`\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularBatcher`](../interfaces/AngularBatcher.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst batcher = injectBatcher(\n  (items) => console.log('Processing batch:', items),\n  { maxSize: 5, wait: 2000 }\n);\n\n// Add items\nbatcher.addItem('task1');\n\n// Access the selected state\nconst { items, isPending } = batcher.state();\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: injectBatcher\ntitle: injectBatcher\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction injectBatcher<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): AngularBatcher<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [batcher/injectBatcher.ts:91](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/batcher/injectBatcher.ts#L91)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages a Batcher instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the Batcher's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThe Batcher collects items and processes them in batches based on configurable conditions:\n- Maximum batch size\n- Time-based batching (process after X milliseconds)\n- Custom batch processing logic via getShouldExecute\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function cancels any pending batch when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```ts\nconst batcher = injectBatcher(fn, {\n  maxSize: 5,\n  onUnmount: (b) => b.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`items`) => `void`\n\n### options?\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularBatcherOptions`](../interfaces/AngularBatcherOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\\> = `{}`\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularBatcher`](../interfaces/AngularBatcher.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst batcher = injectBatcher(\n  (items) => console.log('Processing batch:', items),\n  { maxSize: 5, wait: 2000 }\n);\n\n// Add items\nbatcher.addItem('task1');\n\n// Access the selected state\nconst { items, isPending } = batcher.state();\n```\n"}
